Third-party material in this repository
========================================
Exact upstream commits are recorded as git submodules under upstream/ and in PROVENANCE.txt,
which lists the sha256 of every vendored file next to the upstream path it is a copy of
(tools/provenance.sh verify checks this).

minno-tasks — Project Implicit's open task library.  Yoav Bar-Anan and contributors.
  https://github.com/baranan/minno-tasks   Apache License 2.0 (upstream/minno-tasks/LICENSE)
  Used for: task configs converted into stimuli/*.txt; docs/images/ copied to media/minno/;
  IAT/iat10.js, docs/studies/datapipe.iat.examples/demo.iats/ and docs/studies/raceiat/ as the
  protocol reference.
  Copyright of the photographs: the image files are distributed by minno-tasks under its Apache-2.0
  license; this repository redistributes them unmodified on that basis. If you are a rights-holder
  and believe a file should not be here, open an issue and it will be removed.

minno-time — the Minno task player.  https://github.com/minnojs/minno-time
  Apache License 2.0 (upstream/minno-time/LICENSE).  Used only as the scoring reference
  (src/js/extensions/dscore/parcelMng.js); no code is copied.

stb_image.h — Sean Barrett and contributors.  https://github.com/nothings/stb
  Public domain (Unlicense) or MIT, at your option (see the end of third_party/stb_image.h).

font8x8 — Daniel Hepper, from IBM public-domain VGA fonts.  https://github.com/dhepper/font8x8
  Public domain (third_party/font8x8_basic.h header).

media/project-implicit/ — Project Implicit study materials, from
  https://www.projectimplicit.net/resources/study-materials/ (fetched by tools/fetch_media.ps1).
  Project Implicit makes them available "for academic research purposes" and asks that users cite
  Nosek et al. (2007); it states no redistribution licence.

references/*.pdf — author-posted copies of the papers in references/papers.bib, from
  https://faculty.washington.edu/agg/bydate.htm.  Copyright remains with the publishers.

stimuli/flowers-insects.txt is a demonstration set whose word lists are not taken from a cited source;
see its header.
